Coral and Pearl meet at the Plankton Movie theaters at the ticketing booth
Coral: Hi Pearl, I’m Coral! Loving your blazer by the way.
Pearl: Thank you for your complement. I hope it isn’t too much for a movie, I came here straight from work, and I always like to dress appropriately for any occasion. Please excuse this mishap. Won’t happen again. 
Coral: Not at all, I totally understand. Who has time for a wardrobe change in the middle of the day? Busy gals like us have our fins full already. Trust me, I understand. Marlin and his antics, plus my work and my involvement in coaching. 
Pearl: You do have your fins full. Makes our date more meaningful as you’re here despite having a busy schedule. I appreciate that.
Coral: Lets hurry to the commission stand, this place is packed today!
Coral and Pearl wait to buy popcorn and snacks. 
Coral: Hmm, popcorn is $8, soda is $6, candy is $5 so $19 total and the combo is $3 cheaper. 3/19 is 15.789% so the combo is cheaper and 70% more popcorn. Combo it is. 
Pearl: That’s very impressive you can manage all that math in your head, I like someone with precision and efficiency. And you got Swedish human minis? Those are my favorite gummies. 
Coral: Yeah, I saw you throw away some of their wrappers just now, thought you might like some more! 
Pearl: That’s very thoughtful of you. Detailed oriented, too. I’m surprised you said you stepped back on your senior position. I understand it was scheduling issues when you had Marlin, but you are overqualified for your current role. Have you thought about seeking new jobs?
Coral: Yes, but flexible scheduling with Marlin in mind is hard for a company to accept. 
Pearl: I know today is a date, but I just can’t help seeing a diamond not being appreciated for its worth. I have a position opened at my archive and I think you would be a great fit. Of course it would be flexible with your schedule in mind. Family comes first.
Coral: That’s a very generous offer. I will definitely look the position over, thank you!
After Date
Pearl: I didn’t intend to hire someone on a date, but Coral deserves so much more. Still, I'm still looking for love, not an employee. Send me out on another date.
